-- Umbra — on-ledger participation eligibility (COMP-01, ERC-3643 analog).
--
-- `DeskEligibility` is the on-ledger credential that gates who may participate:
-- an operator/Compliance-signed, per-desk attestation carrying accreditation /
-- jurisdiction / sanctions flags. It is the GATE PRIMITIVE — the actual enforcement
-- (fetch the credential + `assertDeskEligible` inside `Venue.SubmitOrder` /
-- `CommitOrder` and at Holding issuance) lands in 11-05, and the on-ledger
-- REJECTION negative tests land in 11-06. This plan ships the credential template
-- + its `isEligible` predicate + the `assertDeskEligible` gate helper + a positive
-- lifecycle test.
--
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- ENVIRONMENTAL DEVIATION (recorded, honest): CONTRACT KEYS ARE UNAVAILABLE.
-- The plan (11-RESEARCH Pattern 3) specified a keyed template `key (operator, desk)`
-- + `maintainer key._1` + a `fetchByKey @DeskEligibility (operator, desk)` gate. On
-- this stack — Daml SDK 3.4.11 / Canton 3.4 / Daml-LF 2.1 — contract keys are NOT
-- supported by the compiler ("Failure to process Daml program … Contract keys."):
-- Canton 3.x removed unique contract keys, which is why NO template across the prior
-- ten phases uses one (D7 already forbade a key on `Asset`/`Holding` for the split
-- DuplicateKey risk; the deeper reason is the whole LF-2.1 line has no key support).
-- The credential is therefore keyless, and the gate primitive is fetch-by-ContractId
-- + `assertDeskEligible` (the exact D7 Option-B "pass the ContractId explicitly"
-- discipline already used for every Asset/Holding leg in `Round.Clear`). This
-- preserves EVERY security property (a desk still cannot self-issue) and the
-- `isEligible` predicate verbatim — only the lookup mechanism changes from
-- fetchByKey to fetch-by-cid. See 11-02-SUMMARY "Deviations" + "Notes for 11-05".
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
--
-- HONEST STUB BOUNDARY (11-UI-SPEC honesty contract): this is a STUB ATTESTATION
-- issued by the operator/Compliance role — the on-screen label reads
--   STUB ATTESTATION — REAL KYC VENDOR IS TRACK B
-- A real KYC/AML vendor (Refinitiv/Chainalysis-class) is Track B, NOT this phase.
-- No claim is made that `accredited`/`sanctionsClear` reflect a real KYC check; the
-- honest value is that PARTICIPATION IS GATED ON-LEDGER by an authority-signed
-- credential (a desk cannot self-issue — spoofing is structurally impossible).
--
-- Standalone module (no Holding/Auction import) so it compiles independently —
-- Wave-1 parallel-safe with 11-01.
module Umbra.Compliance where

-- The per-desk eligibility credential (ERC-3643 analog). Signed by the operator
-- AND the Compliance role (`compliance` may == `operator` for the MVP stub — a
-- single trust domain), observed by the desk it describes so the desk can see its
-- own standing. A desk is NOT a signatory: it CANNOT forge or self-amend its own
-- eligibility (threat T-11-02-FORGE — mitigated structurally). One stable credential
-- per desk is maintained by the operator/Compliance issuance discipline (no contract
-- key on this line — see the ENVIRONMENTAL DEVIATION note above).
template DeskEligibility
  with
    operator       : Party   -- venue operator (issuer / logical key owner)
    compliance     : Party   -- Compliance role co-signer (may == operator, MVP stub)
    desk           : Party   -- the desk this credential describes (observer only)
    accredited     : Bool    -- accredited/qualified investor attestation (STUB)
    jurisdiction   : Text     -- recorded/observable, NOT a hard gate in the MVP (see isEligible)
    sanctionsClear : Bool    -- sanctions-screening clear attestation (STUB)
  where
    signatory operator, compliance
    observer desk

    -- Withdraw a credential (operator/Compliance authority). Consuming: once revoked
    -- the desk is no longer eligible and a fresh credential must be re-issued. Either
    -- signatory can revoke.
    choice Revoke : ()
      controller operator, compliance
      do pure ()

-- The eligibility predicate (the gate test 11-05 will assert on-ledger).
-- `jurisdiction` is RECORDED and observable but is NOT a hard gate in the MVP stub —
-- the honest gate is accreditation AND sanctions-clear. A production KYC vendor
-- (Track B) would fold jurisdiction/whitelist rules in here.
isEligible : DeskEligibility -> Bool
isEligible e = e.accredited && e.sanctionsClear

-- The GATE PRIMITIVE for 11-05 (the keyless equivalent of the planned
-- `fetchByKey @DeskEligibility (operator, desk)` + `assertMsg (isEligible …)`).
-- 11-05 fetches the credential by ContractId (passed explicitly, D7 Option-B) inside
-- `Venue.SubmitOrder` / `CommitOrder` / the Holding-issuance choice — where operator
-- authority co-flows because `Venue` is `signatory operator` — then calls this:
-- it asserts the credential actually describes THIS (operator, desk) pair (so a
-- credential for another desk cannot be substituted) AND that the desk is eligible.
-- An ineligible or mismatched desk is rejected ON-LEDGER (assertMsg failure), never
-- in render logic.
assertDeskEligible : Party -> Party -> DeskEligibility -> Update ()
assertDeskEligible operator desk cred = do
  assertMsg "eligibility credential does not match (operator, desk)"
    (cred.operator == operator && cred.desk == desk)
  assertMsg "desk not eligible (accreditation/jurisdiction/sanctions)"
    (isEligible cred)
